456
00:38:06,100 --> 00:38:10,280
Sewers will return on Modern Marvels, here on the History Channel.

457
00:38:14,960 --> 00:38:18,440
Even the best-built sewers will break down over time.

458
00:38:18,441 --> 00:38:23,840
strong acids and abrasive debris cause sewers to deteriorate

459
00:38:23,841 --> 00:38:32,300
breaches can lead to leaks leaks can lead to broken pipes and broken pipes can lead to big trouble

460
00:38:32,301 --> 00:38:40,160
maintenance and rehabilitation are key and usually start at the portal to the underground

461
00:38:40,161 --> 00:38:47,620
the manhole manhole covers originated in more in jodaro about 3500 years bce

462
00:38:47,621 --> 00:38:51,480
because even then they knew they were going to have to get into that sewer to clean it.

463
00:38:52,200 --> 00:38:53,140
From there it evolved.

464
00:38:53,580 --> 00:38:56,820
Over time, man has realized no matter what sewer they built,

465
00:38:57,320 --> 00:39:03,100
the Romans, the Parisians, and London, they had access points into their sewers.

466
00:39:03,640 --> 00:39:07,500
They rapidly discovered that round was best because any other shape,

467
00:39:08,040 --> 00:39:13,080
square, rectangular, triangular, if you weren't careful, that would fall down into the sewer.

468
00:39:17,620 --> 00:39:23,620
To prevent catastrophic blockages, ruptures and overflows, various technologies are used.

469
00:39:25,620 --> 00:39:30,620
While the personal expertise of sewer diver Eric Thiel is very valuable to the industry,

470
00:39:31,620 --> 00:39:37,620
robots now inspect thousands of miles of sewers that are inaccessible or too dangerous for humans.

471
00:39:38,620 --> 00:39:45,620
Also known as Responder, this remotely operated vehicle is mostly made of stainless steel and sheet metal.

472
00:39:45,621 --> 00:39:51,940
sheet metal, features rubber molded treads along 38-inch tracks, stands 18 inches high,

473
00:39:51,941 --> 00:39:53,940
and weighs about 500 pounds.

474
00:39:53,941 --> 00:39:59,260
Similar to the Mars Rover, predecessors of this sewer-dwelling machine have been used

475
00:39:59,261 --> 00:40:03,060
to inspect and take samples from Chernobyl and Three Mile Island.

476
00:40:03,061 --> 00:40:07,860
So you know the little guy's tough.

477
00:40:07,861 --> 00:40:13,940
This is a sewer robot that was designed to go into very deep sewer systems, deep tunnel

478
00:40:13,941 --> 00:40:14,940
systems.

479
00:40:14,941 --> 00:40:21,800
The robot can go a mile in distance down a sewer, can go 500 feet underwater,

480
00:40:22,740 --> 00:40:27,120
carries tools in the front of the vehicle to clean the sewer out of the sediment.

481
00:40:28,380 --> 00:40:30,980
They're equipped with a wide array of sensors.

482
00:40:30,981 --> 00:40:40,500
So we use sonar, which is the same way a bat or a dolphin would measure distances to objects in its environment.

483
00:40:41,000 --> 00:40:44,620
And those are used principally for submerged sewer lines.

484
00:40:44,940 --> 00:40:46,760
so sewers that are flooded with water.

485
00:40:47,380 --> 00:40:50,020
For sewers that are dry or mainly damp,

486
00:40:50,021 --> 00:40:54,100
we use lasers, which provide a very precise scanning mechanism

487
00:40:54,101 --> 00:40:57,480
to precisely measure the geometry of sewer pipes and tunnels.

488
00:40:57,700 --> 00:40:58,980
These aren't simple robots.

489
00:40:59,100 --> 00:41:02,480
They're very complex, sometimes even thinking machines.

490
00:41:03,500 --> 00:41:05,280
Smart as this robot is,

491
00:41:05,820 --> 00:41:09,140
engineers aren't ready to let Responder off the leash just yet.

492
00:41:10,420 --> 00:41:12,800
Responder is monitored through its tether,

493
00:41:12,801 --> 00:41:16,840
which provides power down to the robot so that it can move

494
00:41:16,841 --> 00:41:21,540
and also communications telemetry back up to the operator workstation

495
00:41:21,541 --> 00:41:23,920
which is in the truck located near the manholes.

496
00:41:24,360 --> 00:41:27,500
Trained operators will actually instruct the robot to move.

497
00:41:27,660 --> 00:41:32,580
They use a wireless joystick control like you would a Nintendo GameCube that my kids play.

498
00:41:33,000 --> 00:41:37,060
And they also monitor screens which present the sonar and laser information

499
00:41:37,061 --> 00:41:42,760
so they can decide where to move next or where to work or what debris they want to cut out or remove.

500
00:41:42,800 --> 00:41:48,640
These efficient machines get to the root of the problem safely and quickly.

501
00:41:49,820 --> 00:41:52,920
And municipalities have always recognized that time is money.

502
00:41:54,080 --> 00:41:59,640
Traditional technology prior to the 1970s was dig and replace.

503
00:42:00,100 --> 00:42:05,720
This involves using backhoes and operators and workers with shovels working in a trench.

504
00:42:06,360 --> 00:42:08,140
It's obviously a dangerous situation.

505
00:42:08,141 --> 00:42:12,180
It blocks city streets, homes, access to businesses.

506
00:42:12,800 --> 00:42:17,840
A thousand feet of pipe done in the 60s could have taken two to three weeks to rehabilitate.

507
00:42:18,480 --> 00:42:24,720
Using our existing technology, we can rehabilitate that same 1,000 feet in about one day.

508
00:42:25,720 --> 00:42:30,820
An innovative trenchless method that can restore structural integrity to underground pipes

509
00:42:30,821 --> 00:42:33,600
with no digging and no pipe replacement.

510
00:42:34,600 --> 00:42:41,200
The cured-in-place technology takes a felt tube that is saturated with a liquid resin.

511
00:42:41,201 --> 00:42:48,060
it is installed into the sewer pipe underground using water pressure.

512
00:42:48,600 --> 00:42:52,940
The water pressure inverts the tube, turns it inside out,

513
00:42:53,260 --> 00:42:56,960
and at the same time holds it up against the old sewer pipe.

514
00:42:57,820 --> 00:43:01,300
The liquid resin has a catalyst or a hardener in it,

515
00:43:01,301 --> 00:43:06,220
and when the water is heated, the liquid resin becomes hard.

516
00:43:06,221 --> 00:43:11,300
And now you have a liner or a hard pipe inside the old pipe.

517
00:43:12,480 --> 00:43:15,700
Despite the advantages afforded by trenchless technology,

518
00:43:16,360 --> 00:43:19,020
if today's sewer systems are going to stay up to snuff,

519
00:43:19,640 --> 00:43:21,100
they still need a lot of attention,

520
00:43:21,840 --> 00:43:25,380
over $300 billion worth, according to recent studies.

521
00:43:26,200 --> 00:43:31,520
The American Society of Civil Engineers recently graded the effort on rehabilitation

522
00:43:31,521 --> 00:43:36,320
and maintaining our sewer system with a D-, the lowest rating to date.

523
00:43:36,900 --> 00:43:43,240
Usually it takes some type of problem to cause a community to realize what they have to do.

524
00:43:43,241 --> 00:43:48,060
Then all of a sudden, sewers are on their mind, and they take the initiative and the effort

525
00:43:48,061 --> 00:43:51,700
and start spending the money to get the crews, the equipment, the machinery

526
00:43:51,701 --> 00:43:54,300
to maintain and rebuild their sewers.

527
00:43:54,880 --> 00:43:59,720
There's tens of thousands of miles of these sewer systems out there that need work,

528
00:43:59,840 --> 00:44:00,920
and they need work soon.

529
00:44:01,520 --> 00:44:02,920
or they may stop functioning.

530
00:44:04,240 --> 00:44:06,920
And while we prefer to just flush and forget,

531
00:44:07,540 --> 00:44:10,800
we'd better remember how much sewer systems have evolved

532
00:44:10,801 --> 00:44:15,280
and how vital they are to our continued health and comfort.

533
00:44:17,300 --> 00:44:19,160
Imagine the alternative.

